{"type":"assistant.message","data":{"messageId":"a14529bf-907a-4fee-9cc0-d1c7aceef703","content":"Progress: I inspected your repo and opened the client/server `package.json` files. Next I'll explain likely causes and give concrete fixes you can run now.\n\n- **Found:** [OpenGlimpse_reference/src/server/package.json](OpenGlimpse_reference/src/server/package.json) and [OpenGlimpse_reference/src/client/package.json](OpenGlimpse_reference/src/client/package.json) (also same files under `OpenGlimpse/src/...`).\n- **Likely cause:** Node/npm look for `package.json` in the current working directory. If you start the server or client from the workspace root (or a different folder), the runtime won't find the expected `package.json` under `src/server` or `src/client`.\n- **Quick manual fix:** run install/start commands from the correct folder.\n  - Server:\n    ```bash\n    cd OpenGlimpse_reference/src/server\n    npm install\n    npm run start\n    ```\n  - Client (Vite):\n    ```bash\n    cd OpenGlimpse_reference/src/client\n    npm install\n    npm run dev\n    ```\n- **Recommended: root script to run both:** create a root `package.json` (at `OpenGlimpse_reference/package.json`) that delegates to the correct subfolders. Example:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"name\": \"openglimpse-root\",\n    \"private\": true,\n    \"scripts\": {\n      \"install:all\": \"npm --prefix src/server install && npm --prefix src/client install\",\n      \"start:server\": \"npm --prefix src/server run start\",\n      \"start:client\": \"npm --prefix src/client run dev\",\n      \"start\": \"concurrently \\\"npm run start:server\\\" \\\"npm run start:client\\\"\"\n    },\n    \"devDependencies\": {\n      \"concurrently\": \"^8.0.0\"\n    }\n  }\n  ```\n  Then from repo root:\n  ```bash\n  npm install\n  npm run install:all\n  npm run start\n  ```\n- **VS Code / launch config:** if you use debug/launch tasks, set `cwd` to the subfolder you want (for server launch use `OpenGlimpse_reference/src/server`) 